WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.334 --> 00:00:01.435
- Can I get a clap from Buck?

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.469
Excellent, Buck.

00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:05.472
And we go live in three, two.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.809
- My name is Annie Roth,
and I am a journalist

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.978
on assignment
with National Geographic.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.145
- My name is Melissa Márquez.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.015
I'm a shark scientist
aboard the "Ocean Explorer."

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.451
- And like Melissa said, we are
aboard the "Ocean Explorer,"

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.888
which is a huge vessel dedicated
to science and media production.

00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:22.456
Right now, we're in mission control,

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.358
watching a remotely operated vehicle

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.627
sending down to--
what have we got?

00:00:27.928 --> 00:00:29.263
[speaking indistinctly]

00:00:29.296 --> 00:00:30.631
- To 231 meters.

00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:33.567
- 231 meters,
and we're watching two submersibles

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.638
that are already down on the bottom
that are there to study six-gilled sharks,

00:00:37.671 --> 00:00:39.873
the biggest deep-sea shark out there.

00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:45.145
And they already have some fish down there
and a tube filled with chum.

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:47.915
And we're just playing the waiting game,
hoping for these sharks to show up.

00:00:47.948 --> 00:00:49.550
We've already seen two of them.

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:52.119
And we're hoping
that another one shows up.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.954
And yeah, are you excited?

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.757
- Yeah. Very excited.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.560
- We've been up for a couple hours,
so bear with us.

00:00:59.593 --> 00:01:02.696
And meet our awesome ROV pilots.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.565
- I am Olaf.

00:01:04.598 --> 00:01:06.767
- And I'm Euan Bason.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.570
- We've also got one of our
sub pilots over here.

00:01:09.603 --> 00:01:12.005
- I am, uh, Buck Taylor.

00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:13.574
- Did you forget your name?

00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:14.675
[laughter]

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:17.778
- It's been a long night.
- I know.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:21.481
- So sharks are nocturnal, and so is
the crew of the "Ocean Explorer"

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:23.383
for the next couple days.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:26.286
And yeah, it's taken a toll,
to be honest with you.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.055
[laughter]

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.290
But right now, there are two subs down,

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:32.192
and there are three people
in each of them.

00:01:32.226 --> 00:01:36.463
And they are hoping to see the six-gills
because they are conducting

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.399
not only a ambitious filmmaking project
to film

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:42.436
these sharks in their natural habitat;
they're also trying to tag them.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:46.507
So their goal is to attach
two different kinds of tags

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:52.346
to the six-gill sharks here
to learn about their vertical migration

00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:55.282
or distribution,
how they spend their time.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.850
They want to know what they're up to.

00:01:56.884 --> 00:02:00.487
They want to know how climate change
is impacting them.

00:02:00.521 --> 00:02:02.456
They want to know
what they're eating

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.957
and just, like,
what they're doing with their time.

00:02:03.991 --> 00:02:05.492
Who doesn't want to know?
These sharks are awesome.

00:02:05.526 --> 00:02:08.028
Of course we want to know
what they're doing.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.663
Yeah.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.598
Anything else
you want to say about sharks?

00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:13.467
- No, you've taken everything
out of my mouth.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.435
[laughter]

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:18.705
- These sharks are super cool.
They can grow up to 20 feet long.

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:21.175
They can get as big
as great white sharks.

00:02:21.208 --> 00:02:24.678
They haven't changed much since
they shared the planet with dinosaurs.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.813
They have, like, really cool eyes.

00:02:26.847 --> 00:02:28.982
They have, like,
really small dorsal fins,

00:02:29.016 --> 00:02:30.617
like, way in the back of their body.

00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:32.586
They're not like your typical shark.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:35.055
And they're kind of the kings down here.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.258
Their only predators are each other
and queens, hey.

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:42.329
- We're seeing females.
They're the queens.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.766
- And yeah, the subs have had a lot
of luck seeing these sharks

00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:47.334
over the past couple days.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.337
And they've even,
like, bumped into the sub.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.675
So yeah, there's been
some fun shark activity.

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:56.577
And we're hoping to see some more here.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.179
Right now, we're just looking at, like,
a bunch of horse mackerel.

00:02:59.213 --> 00:03:01.448
And we saw an eel earlier.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:06.820
So just keep your eyes stuck to the feed,
and you might see something neat.

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.824
You know, if you like fish,
then you came to the right place.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.694
We are on the Condor seamount,

00:03:13.727 --> 00:03:16.430
which is a protected seamount
here in the Azores,

00:03:16.463 --> 00:03:18.432
which is 800 miles off the coast
of Portugal.

00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:20.367
It's an island archipelago.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.138
And the reason we've come here is,
there are a ton of these sharks.

00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:29.276
Fishing for these sharks here
was banned several years ago.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.044
And this particular seamount
is protected,

00:03:31.078 --> 00:03:33.580
so the population here is just thriving.

00:03:33.614 --> 00:03:35.215
And it's no coincidence

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:38.051
that every night these subs
have been down, they've seen one.

00:03:38.085 --> 00:03:41.522
And it's a sign of a really healthy
ecosystem overall here.

00:03:41.555 --> 00:03:43.891
When there's a bunch of top predators,

00:03:43.924 --> 00:03:47.794
it just speaks volumes about the health
of the entire ecosystem.

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:51.765
Yeah, it's fun to see.
I'm having a great time.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.468
Definitely not tired at all.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.403
[laughter]

00:04:01.041 --> 00:04:04.011
- Guys down there are playing
the waiting game, that's for sure.

00:04:04.044 --> 00:04:05.078
- Mm.

00:04:05.112 --> 00:04:08.549
- Yeah, the people in sub have been
down there for quite some time.

00:04:08.582 --> 00:04:13.053
But they brought some snacks, keep them
entertained and fed, so that's good.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.354
- There's card games.

00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:17.491
- Yeah. We've got the two subs,
"Nadir" and "Neptune."

00:04:17.524 --> 00:04:19.960
"Neptune's" a science sub.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.496
So we have two scientists
on board or on pilot.

00:04:22.529 --> 00:04:25.432
And then "Nadir" is our filming sub.

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:28.669
We have a director,
cameraman, and a pilot.

00:04:28.702 --> 00:04:30.537
And so you can't see "Nadir"
at the moment.

00:04:30.571 --> 00:04:33.006
She's in the dark,
hiding out of the way.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.577
And I've been piloting
the last few nights.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.245
I'm out tonight.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:42.149
But just to see those sharks--
we've spent a lot of time last few days

00:04:42.182 --> 00:04:45.786
just to see those sharks cruise by,

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:47.821
and cruising is--it's impressive,
isn't it?

00:04:47.855 --> 00:04:49.122
- It's amazing.

00:04:49.156 --> 00:04:54.027
I mean, it really is like
looking at a dinosaur, essentially,

00:04:54.061 --> 00:04:56.530
just a dinosaur of the deep.

00:04:56.563 --> 00:04:57.898
They're absolutely--
- Shark.

00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:00.467
- Oh!
- Yeah, here he comes.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.703
- Coming in bottom left, bottom left.

00:05:02.736 --> 00:05:04.505
- There she goes.

00:05:04.538 --> 00:05:06.673
- Look at you.
- Wow.

00:05:06.707 --> 00:05:08.976
- Slow moving but so powerful.

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.310
- Wow.

00:05:10.344 --> 00:05:12.079
- They get their nose under the sub.
- Oh, oh, oh.

00:05:12.112 --> 00:05:14.648
- So this is a 12-meter-wide sub.
- Come on, come on, come on.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:17.017
Come on. Come on.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.953
- Oh, boy.
- Go! Come on, baby. Come on.

00:05:19.987 --> 00:05:22.689
- So the sub that the shark
is in front of is a science sub.

00:05:22.723 --> 00:05:26.560
So there is two spears--spearguns
mounted on the top

00:05:26.593 --> 00:05:30.731
that are armed with tags, which is how
they're trying tag these sharks.

00:05:30.764 --> 00:05:34.601
This shark didn't get quite in range,
but look how huge it is.

00:05:34.635 --> 00:05:36.603
The sub is, like, 12 feet across.

00:05:36.637 --> 00:05:40.340
And so you can kind of see
by perspective how big this shark is.

00:05:40.374 --> 00:05:43.410
- Well, that tube on the seafloor
is 1.8 meters long.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.578
- Yeah.

00:05:44.611 --> 00:05:46.547
So what the scientists are waiting for--

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:50.150
we have two green lasers
that shine out from the sub,

00:05:50.184 --> 00:05:52.553
and they're in line
with the two spearguns.

00:05:52.586 --> 00:05:55.822
And they're waiting for that to go
just below the dorsal--

00:05:55.856 --> 00:05:58.458
or just below the sort of lateral line

00:05:58.492 --> 00:06:02.029
or above the lateral line
into the sort of muscle there.

00:06:02.062 --> 00:06:06.700
So this is tough for the guys, you know,
moving the sub around quickly.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:09.803
And so they have to sit
and wait for that shark--

00:06:09.837 --> 00:06:11.505
- Come back around.
- Come on, baby.

00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:13.073
Come on.
- Wow.

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:15.008
- And so they're very patient,
these guys.

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:17.611
They'll just sit and wait
and get the perfect shot.

00:06:17.644 --> 00:06:20.247
- For hours and hours.
- Hours and hours.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.616
- We run out of snacks. We cry a little.

00:06:22.649 --> 00:06:24.751
- And you've been in that sub.
It weighs a ton.

00:06:24.785 --> 00:06:26.587
But when they want to move the sub,

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.855
they'll move the sub, won't they,
the sharks?

00:06:27.888 --> 00:06:29.389
- Yeah, yeah, oh, 100%.

00:06:29.423 --> 00:06:32.593
- They'll put their nose underneath
and just push you around.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:37.431
- It's a bit funny
how easy these sharks move.

00:06:37.464 --> 00:06:39.800
- Hold on. Come back around.

00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:41.935
What's--from the bottom--

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:44.037
No, wait. Where is it?

00:06:44.071 --> 00:06:45.939
- It's just underneath us.
- Oh, it's underneath us.

00:06:45.973 --> 00:06:47.808
- The sharks have been doing this
every night.

00:06:47.841 --> 00:06:50.444
They'll pick up the scent
and start circling round

00:06:50.477 --> 00:06:54.515
and gradually hone in
and work out where the bait is.

00:06:54.548 --> 00:06:56.617
So--
- It disappeared.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.985
- It's underneath us.

00:06:58.018 --> 00:06:59.386
- It's just underneath us.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:02.055
- No, it's disappeared, you guys.
It sucked it up.

00:07:02.089 --> 00:07:04.358
Do you remember how I said that you were
gonna do, like, alien abduction stuff?

00:07:04.391 --> 00:07:06.693
You've alien abducted the shark.

00:07:06.727 --> 00:07:09.763
So if you're just tuning in,
we just saw a--

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.865
[laughter]

00:07:11.899 --> 00:07:15.002
We just saw a six-gill shark,
and we are watching--

00:07:15.035 --> 00:07:16.436
- Wait, hold on a second.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:17.871
- Oh, come on, baby.
- Incoming.

00:07:17.905 --> 00:07:19.072
- Here we go.
- No, get closer.

00:07:19.106 --> 00:07:20.474
- He's picking up that scent.

00:07:20.507 --> 00:07:21.642
- Get closer.

00:07:21.675 --> 00:07:23.410
- So they can't just tag the shark
anywhere.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:28.882
It has to be in the perfect,
like, spot on its back.

00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:30.450
- Oh, come on.
- Here--oh, oh.

00:07:30.484 --> 00:07:32.352
- No, no.

00:07:32.386 --> 00:07:33.353
Come on.
- Wow.

00:07:33.387 --> 00:07:35.856
- If he turns to the left now--
- Turn, turn, turn.

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:37.224
- Turn, turn.

00:07:37.257 --> 00:07:39.860
- She's gonna go to the vapor.
There's fish on the vapor.

00:07:39.893 --> 00:07:42.429
Up her nose.
- Of course she is.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.598
- Wow, the sub's
getting a real show right now.

00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:48.435
- So the three guys in the sub,
they'll have a front view.

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:50.671
- He just booped the sub.
- Yeah.

00:07:50.704 --> 00:07:52.673
- Oh, my God. Oh!

00:07:52.706 --> 00:07:53.707
- Wow.
- That's a big shark.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.977
- Look at that!
- Okay. Just go off, I guess.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:00.314
- To give you an idea of size,
that's four meters.

00:08:00.347 --> 00:08:02.549
- Wow. Four meters.
- Yeah.

00:08:02.583 --> 00:08:05.219
Wow, that was such
a dramatic shot just now.

00:08:05.252 --> 00:08:06.753
- That's about max size for them,
isn't it, Buck?

00:08:06.787 --> 00:08:09.756
- Sorry?
- 20 feet is about max size for them.

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.791
- Wow.

00:08:10.824 --> 00:08:14.261
- That we know of, yeah.
So on average, they're 14, 18.

00:08:14.294 --> 00:08:16.196
- Yeah, they get a little bit
bigger than that, but yeah.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.699
- Yeah.
- Wow. Oh, turn around.

00:08:18.732 --> 00:08:19.833
- Here she comes again.
- Coming back.

00:08:19.867 --> 00:08:20.901
- There she goes.
- Come on.

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.369
- It's all about that scent.

00:08:22.402 --> 00:08:23.804
And you can see her eyeball.
- Oh, you can see her eye.

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:25.038
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:08:25.072 --> 00:08:26.773
- Those eyes are amazing.

00:08:26.807 --> 00:08:28.408
They just roll around in their head.

00:08:28.442 --> 00:08:30.477
- Oh, my goodness.

00:08:30.511 --> 00:08:33.413
- Beautiful shark.
- They are.

00:08:33.447 --> 00:08:37.417
- The tags they're trying to attach
to the shark will allow scientists to--

00:08:37.451 --> 00:08:38.986
- There she goes.
- Oh!

00:08:39.019 --> 00:08:41.088
- Come on, baby girl.

00:08:41.121 --> 00:08:42.923
Come on. Yes, come on.

00:08:42.956 --> 00:08:44.091
- If she turns...
- Turn, turn, turn.

00:08:44.124 --> 00:08:45.225
- Oh, boy!

00:08:45.259 --> 00:08:47.027
both: Turn, turn, turn.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.896
- Now, so the problem is, we have to…

00:08:48.929 --> 00:08:50.063
- She's just teasing the sub.

00:08:50.097 --> 00:08:54.902
- Place that bait, but I think there's
a bag of fish blood in that corner.

00:08:54.935 --> 00:08:55.836
- Yes.

00:08:55.869 --> 00:08:57.571
- And so she's--
- Oh, yeah, that's true.

00:08:57.604 --> 00:09:01.175
- Her nose is very, very, good.
She knows exactly where that is.

00:09:01.208 --> 00:09:02.676
- Well, imagine being in the sub
right now.

00:09:02.709 --> 00:09:05.579
They're really getting
the full experience.

00:09:05.612 --> 00:09:07.147
- We've had that.

00:09:07.181 --> 00:09:10.083
It's pretty amazing,
them getting that close and--

00:09:10.117 --> 00:09:12.019
- Oh, she got it.
Got the bag.

00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:13.287
[laughter]

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.355
- That's it.
We're never seeing that bag again.

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:16.690
[laughter]

00:09:16.723 --> 00:09:18.725
- We'll pick it up before we go, though,
won't we, Buck?

00:09:18.759 --> 00:09:21.461
- It's well protected.
She can't get hold of it.

00:09:21.495 --> 00:09:22.896
- There she goes.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.464
I don't think she's done with us yet.

00:09:24.498 --> 00:09:27.968
- A little bit of a tease,
but we do leave some behind.

00:09:28.001 --> 00:09:31.004
Well, they normally will pick bits
off the bar.

00:09:31.038 --> 00:09:32.039
- There she goes.

00:09:32.072 --> 00:09:33.907
- What a beautiful fish.
- Wow.

00:09:33.941 --> 00:09:35.742
- Great shot, Jeremy.
- Yeah.

00:09:35.776 --> 00:09:37.644
- Wow.
- That is stunning.

00:09:39.213 --> 00:09:40.581
- Oh, little bit of a turn.
- Oh, she's turning.

00:09:40.614 --> 00:09:42.115
- Oh!
- Come on.

00:09:42.149 --> 00:09:44.418
- She can't get enough.
- Yeah.

00:09:44.451 --> 00:09:47.454
And they've been doing this every night.
They come in.

00:09:47.487 --> 00:09:50.090
They have a sniff, a nibble,
and then they'll pull away again

00:09:50.123 --> 00:09:54.494
and might get spooked with all the lights
and they'll just cruise back in again.

00:09:54.528 --> 00:09:56.430
Great work with the ROV, guys.

00:09:56.463 --> 00:09:59.867
- We're getting so lucky
with this renowned huge shark.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.970
Really just, you know,
so interested in the bait.

00:10:03.003 --> 00:10:05.772
You must have really stabbed it up good.

00:10:05.806 --> 00:10:07.774
- Yes.
- [laughs]

00:10:10.077 --> 00:10:12.913
- She's just cruising
on the edge of the lights.

00:10:16.383 --> 00:10:19.353
- But yeah, scientists want to--
oh, what's going on?

00:10:19.386 --> 00:10:21.154
- Just on the starboard side.
Here she comes.

00:10:21.188 --> 00:10:22.789
She's gonna come in from the--
- Another shark?

00:10:22.823 --> 00:10:25.125
- No, it's the same one.
- Same one. She's just turning.

00:10:25.158 --> 00:10:26.293
- Yeah.

00:10:26.326 --> 00:10:30.264
- So yeah, scientists want to attach a tag
to this shark that will--

00:10:30.297 --> 00:10:31.565
- She's coming in high.

00:10:31.598 --> 00:10:34.134
- Coming behind the sub, yeah.
- Okay, coming left.

00:10:35.302 --> 00:10:39.740
- Scientists want to put a camera tag
and a satellite tag on these sharks.

00:10:39.773 --> 00:10:42.576
Allow them to see what they're doing,

00:10:42.609 --> 00:10:46.847
where they're spending their time,
what they're eating.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.518
All kinds of things that we have not
really been able to study

00:10:51.552 --> 00:10:53.921
because of how inaccessible
these sharks are.

00:10:53.954 --> 00:10:56.290
- How important are they
to the ecosystem?

00:10:58.158 --> 00:10:59.293
- Take it away, shark expert.

00:10:59.326 --> 00:11:02.462
- No, you've been doing a great job.

