00:23:17.097 --> 00:23:20.834
- Yeah. Olaf, explain what it does
to your instruments,

00:23:20.868 --> 00:23:23.604
you know, when you've got
that many fish in your--

00:23:24.771 --> 00:23:27.174
- Well, we have a altimeter
on the bottom--

00:23:27.207 --> 00:23:29.176
or a DVL on the bottom of that ROV,

00:23:29.209 --> 00:23:31.578
and if fish swim underneath,
it does, like,

00:23:31.612 --> 00:23:34.615
tend to give us a false return
on the acoustics,

00:23:34.648 --> 00:23:39.086
so it can push the ROV off into
a different direction

00:23:39.119 --> 00:23:43.524
[indistinct]
or give us a false return on a altitude,

00:23:43.557 --> 00:23:48.295
which then can kick us up or down. Yes.

00:23:48.328 --> 00:23:50.831
- I got shouted at by Buck
for coming down too quickly.

00:23:50.864 --> 00:23:51.932
[laughter]

00:23:51.965 --> 00:23:53.467
Come down five meters.
- That's because--

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:55.536
- That's not five meters!

00:23:55.569 --> 00:24:00.407
- That's 'cause they think you're gonna
squish the sphere when we see your--

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:03.477
everybody thinks of an ROV
as quite a small vehicle,

00:24:03.510 --> 00:24:09.516
but imagine a minivan
coming at you at 20 miles an hour

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:11.885
and you're sat on the bottom of the seabed

00:24:11.919 --> 00:24:14.721
in this delicate little plastic sphere.

00:24:14.755 --> 00:24:18.158
And you know that Olaf
and Euan are upstairs

00:24:18.192 --> 00:24:20.294
with big smiles on their faces.

00:24:20.327 --> 00:24:21.728
[laughter]

00:24:21.762 --> 00:24:24.198
It adds to the excitement, anyway.

00:24:25.499 --> 00:24:28.869
- ROV, stop.
- Stop, stop, stop.

00:24:28.902 --> 00:24:30.470
[laughter]

00:24:30.504 --> 00:24:31.638
- And the bag is full.

00:24:31.672 --> 00:24:34.174
[laughter]

00:24:34.208 --> 00:24:36.176
- So where are these sharks? Come on.

00:24:36.210 --> 00:24:39.947
- Yeah, sharks.
Giving us a little tease.

00:24:39.980 --> 00:24:42.216
If you missed it before,
there were two huge sharks.

00:24:42.249 --> 00:24:45.018
We're not bluffing. They were here.

00:24:45.052 --> 00:24:47.221
So we're just playing the waiting game

00:24:47.254 --> 00:24:49.723
and keeping an eye out for anything else
that wants to show up.

00:24:49.756 --> 00:24:52.926
The past couple nights,
random animals have shown up.

00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:58.966
There was a mola mola just hanging out,
which was quite a sight to see at depth.

00:24:58.999 --> 00:25:02.503
And yeah, I want to see
some more sharks, though,

00:25:02.536 --> 00:25:06.473
'cause they're kind of
what's popping down here.

00:25:06.507 --> 00:25:09.309
- Yeah. I think the most amazing scene
this week

00:25:09.343 --> 00:25:14.348
was, I was sat in the media sub filming,
looking up, seeing the other sub

00:25:14.381 --> 00:25:17.918
and the ROV,
which is pretty amazing anyway.

00:25:17.951 --> 00:25:19.820
And you get this whole arena.

00:25:19.853 --> 00:25:23.190
And as you say,
the mola mola just gliding in.

00:25:23.223 --> 00:25:24.591
And then a six-gill underneath.

00:25:24.625 --> 00:25:28.795
And you have to pinch yourself
because it's just completely unreal.

00:25:28.829 --> 00:25:32.866
- That's so cool.
- Yeah, absolutely amazing.

00:25:32.900 --> 00:25:36.003
We're in a special place here.
Really are.

00:25:37.004 --> 00:25:40.040
- Yeah, it's no coincidence that
there's so much awesome life here.

00:25:40.073 --> 00:25:44.044
The protections for this particular
seamount, the Condor seamount,

00:25:44.077 --> 00:25:46.880
and the surrounding waters
are really good.

00:25:46.914 --> 00:25:50.384
And so when you protect marine ecosystems,
this is what you get.

00:25:50.417 --> 00:25:53.687
Tons of fish, tons of sharks.
Perfect balance.

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:56.190
Sometimes so many fish
that you can't see the sharks.

00:25:56.223 --> 00:26:00.460
But that's fine 'cause that's what we want
to see when we're not filming, I guess.

00:26:00.494 --> 00:26:01.828
- We prefer it that way.

00:26:01.862 --> 00:26:03.096
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:26:03.130 --> 00:26:05.165
- Even if it makes filming
a little more difficult.

00:26:05.199 --> 00:26:10.304
- Very often, we'll get to seamounts
and all you'll find is very little life

00:26:10.337 --> 00:26:12.940
and just fishing gear
everywhere on the bottom.

00:26:12.973 --> 00:26:15.676
And it's just--it's soul-destroying.

00:26:15.709 --> 00:26:16.710
- And litter.

00:26:16.743 --> 00:26:18.846
- Yeah, litter--beer bottles...
- Pick up your litter.

00:26:18.879 --> 00:26:24.117
- Plastic and--yeah, it's--
whereas this is amazing.

00:26:24.151 --> 00:26:26.119
Yeah. Beautiful.

00:26:26.153 --> 00:26:28.322
- Mm-hmm.

00:26:28.355 --> 00:26:30.224
Worth staying up late for.

00:26:30.257 --> 00:26:32.860
- Yeah, definitely.

00:26:36.697 --> 00:26:43.170
Yeah, those guys will be probably
getting into the chocolate stash by now.

00:26:43.203 --> 00:26:47.574
And they've got their--they've had
their evening meal

00:26:47.608 --> 00:26:50.310
which Kirstie and the girls
would have prepared.

00:26:51.545 --> 00:26:57.084
But they'll be getting five into the
chocolate and playing the waiting game.

00:26:57.117 --> 00:26:59.987
- How good is the meal
on board the subs?

00:27:00.020 --> 00:27:01.755
- How good?
It's a meal. It's great.

00:27:01.788 --> 00:27:04.591
- It's amazing.

00:27:04.625 --> 00:27:08.629
- The people who go in the subs
bring plenty of snacks

00:27:08.662 --> 00:27:10.831
'cause they're down there for a while,

00:27:10.864 --> 00:27:15.435
and, you know, watching sharks eat chum
I guess makes you hungry.

00:27:15.469 --> 00:27:18.438
- It's not the healthiest environment
because you just sit there

00:27:18.472 --> 00:27:22.376
and eat food all day and you don't
actually move very much, so...

00:27:26.747 --> 00:27:27.581
- All right.

00:27:27.614 --> 00:27:30.884
- Just need those sharks
to pick up on the scent trail now.

00:27:32.486 --> 00:27:35.489
- Why don't you zoom in on the seafloor
a little bit?

00:27:35.522 --> 00:27:38.091
We can talk about the corals.

00:27:38.125 --> 00:27:40.294
Is that possible?

00:27:40.327 --> 00:27:41.361
- What? Corals?

00:27:41.395 --> 00:27:43.664
- Yeah.
- Yeah, we can just zoom in on that.

00:27:43.697 --> 00:27:46.533
- So yeah, if you see
those long thin strands

00:27:46.567 --> 00:27:48.802
coming from the seabed,
those are whip corals.

00:27:48.836 --> 00:27:52.039
And then the yellow ones
I believe are sea fans.

00:27:52.072 --> 00:27:54.107
There's a purple sponge
down there somewhere.

00:27:54.141 --> 00:27:55.843
I lost track of it, but, like,

00:27:55.876 --> 00:27:57.945
you guys have your eyes
on the screen.

00:27:57.978 --> 00:28:01.081
Find it.

00:28:01.114 --> 00:28:03.684
- It's actually right by--it's right by
the chum flute there somewhere,

00:28:03.717 --> 00:28:04.952
that purple one is.

00:28:04.985 --> 00:28:07.054
- Oh, yeah.

00:28:07.087 --> 00:28:10.991
- And don't worry about what you see with
the plastic drum and the plastic tube.

00:28:11.024 --> 00:28:14.127
Everything we take down,
we bring back up again.

00:28:14.161 --> 00:28:17.564
And very often, we'll bring trash
back up with us if we see it

00:28:17.598 --> 00:28:21.535
and we've got space to put it
on the subs or the ROVs, so....

00:28:21.568 --> 00:28:22.669
- Yeah.

00:28:22.703 --> 00:28:25.439
- We generally bring back more
than we take down.

00:28:25.472 --> 00:28:28.408
- The ROVs and the subs
have mechanical arms

00:28:28.442 --> 00:28:31.879
that they can use to pick stuff up
and pass stuff to each other,

00:28:31.912 --> 00:28:34.414
which is very funny to see, honestly.

00:28:34.448 --> 00:28:37.851
- Can you give us a wave with your arm?
- I can give you a wave with the arm.

00:28:37.885 --> 00:28:39.953
- Oh, yeah.

00:28:39.987 --> 00:28:41.588
- Try not to scratch the camera lens.

00:28:41.622 --> 00:28:44.258
- Without scratching the camera lens.
- Yeah.

00:28:44.291 --> 00:28:48.295
- Maybe we should bring
the camera in a little bit.

00:28:48.328 --> 00:28:52.165
- See, Jamie's gonna shout at me now
for suggesting that 'cause he's--

00:28:52.199 --> 00:28:55.002
- Well, we just need to retract it
on its tray a little bit.

00:28:55.035 --> 00:28:57.738
- Yeah.
And you know this is when the shark--

00:28:57.771 --> 00:29:00.307
- The shark will come.
- Exactly.

00:29:00.340 --> 00:29:03.610
- Zooming out and straightening up.

00:29:03.644 --> 00:29:08.549
- So each of the subs have one arm each,
but the ROV has two arms.

00:29:10.384 --> 00:29:12.586
- Do you want to--turn the head in.
[indistinct radio chatter]

00:29:12.619 --> 00:29:14.888
Keep the camera in the light.

00:29:14.922 --> 00:29:18.559
- That's just the subs talking there,
so...

00:29:18.592 --> 00:29:20.127
What's that, Lee?

00:29:21.228 --> 00:29:23.130
- Zoom out.

00:29:23.163 --> 00:29:24.865
- Was it shark or not?

00:29:24.898 --> 00:29:28.202
- Mm?
- Any sharky or not?

00:29:28.235 --> 00:29:32.573
- He's asking for permission
to turn on the ROV lights.

00:29:32.606 --> 00:29:34.174
- Oh, okay.

00:29:34.208 --> 00:29:36.677
[indistinct radio chatter]

00:29:36.710 --> 00:29:38.745
That's the--you can hear
in the background

00:29:38.779 --> 00:29:42.549
the two subs talking to each other.

00:29:42.583 --> 00:29:45.285
And then we can talk to them
in mission control.

00:29:45.319 --> 00:29:49.356
And then we also have a tracking system
so we know where the two subs are.

00:29:49.389 --> 00:29:54.661
We know where the ROV is and the ship

00:29:54.695 --> 00:30:00.367
can follow all the different assets
around the seabed.

00:30:00.400 --> 00:30:02.002
- What's that?

00:30:02.035 --> 00:30:04.104
- What are we looking at?
- Zoom in center.

00:30:04.137 --> 00:30:06.273
Hold on, there's, like, a--
oh, maybe it's gone.

00:30:06.306 --> 00:30:08.242
It was, like, a very long fish.

00:30:10.410 --> 00:30:12.346
Maybe my eyes were just
playing tricks on me.

00:30:12.379 --> 00:30:15.282
- No, gonna wait until the arm's moved.

00:30:15.315 --> 00:30:19.219
- So we're coming up towards the end
of our time together.

00:30:19.253 --> 00:30:22.122
So if you stumbled upon this,
thanks for watching.

00:30:22.155 --> 00:30:25.325
And if you appreciate sharks and fish
as much as we do,

00:30:25.359 --> 00:30:28.061
then you're really cool;
we should hang out.

00:30:28.095 --> 00:30:30.831
- And Euan's just gonna give us
a little wave with his arm.

00:30:30.864 --> 00:30:32.966
Does that mean it's a goodbye wave?

00:30:36.336 --> 00:30:38.172
- There it is.
- There it is.

00:30:38.205 --> 00:30:40.240
- Hey!
- The claw.

00:30:40.274 --> 00:30:43.443
[laughter]

00:30:43.477 --> 00:30:45.612
- Aw.
- There you go.

00:30:45.646 --> 00:30:48.081
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

